interpretation: getUpdates is an HTTPS request the bot opens to api.telegram.org and Telegram holds open for up to `timeout` seconds; the answer travels back on that same outbound connection, so the NAT's connection tracking delivers it and no inbound port is needed. setWebhook makes Telegram open the connection to a public HTTPS URL on 443/80/88/8443, which a host behind home NAT cannot offer without a port-forward, a tunnel, or a relay.
